# Project contract

Local-first Kaggle cell-tracking infrastructure. Milestones 0–1 only are implemented.

## What exists

- CLI `biohub-track`: `inspect`, `validate-data`, `validate-submission`, `run` (Milestone 2 detection).
- Metadata-first Zarr reader; GEFF annotation discovery; strict submission writer/validator.
- Milestone 2: blob detector produces node-only graphs. Tracker/division are Milestone 3.

## Graph / submission

- Every detection is its own `node_id` (unique per dataset; may restart next dataset).
- Continuity and divisions are directed edges only; division = one source, two outgoing edges.
- Columns: `id,dataset,row_type,node_id,t,z,y,x,source_id,target_id`.
- Node coords are integer voxels `(z,y,x)`; distances use physical coords from metadata spacing.
- Numeric submission columns must be NumPy `int64`.

## Hard gates

- Do not invent Zarr shapes, axes, spacing, annotation schema, or dtypes — discover via `inspect`.
- Do not start Milestone 2 detector until `validate-data` passes on the official download under `data/competition`.
- YAML numeric params are hypotheses until tuned on training data.
- Synthetic fixture under `data/sample` is for infrastructure tests only.
